{"timestamp": 1779388998.20818, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I reported Eve\u2019s body in Electrical. My route was Navigation -> Security -> Electrical, and I didn\u2019t see anyone on the way. As soon as I got into Electrical I found Eve dead and reported immediately. I don\u2019t know where Bob died or who was near him."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389010.633595, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was on the left side of the ship this whole round, mostly doing tasks in Upper Engine and Oxygen. I didn't see Eve or Bob at all, so I can't give any info on who was near them. Alice, since you came from Security to Electrical, did you notice anyone hanging around Security or Storage earlier? We need to piece together where the killer went after dropping Eve. Since we have two bodies, it might have been a fast double or the killer has been busy. I'll be listening to Charlie and Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389025.753439, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started in Oxygen, then went Upper Engine, then Lower Engine. I saw Bob in Oxygen early for a few ticks, and then around tick 6 I saw Bob leave Upper Engine toward Medbay. After that I didn\u2019t see him again, and I never saw Eve.\n\nThe thing that stands out to me is Diana saying she was mostly Upper Engine and Oxygen but didn\u2019t see Bob at all \u2014 because Bob was definitely in Oxygen early and passed through Upper Engine toward Medbay. Could be timing, but it\u2019s a little weird.\n\nFor Eve, Alice finding her in Electrical lines up with someone moving through Medbay/Electrical side, and Bob was last seen heading Medbay, so that area is important. I want to hear Frank\u2019s route, but right now Diana\u2019s statement doesn\u2019t match what I saw."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389051.7652311, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I didn\u2019t see anyone this round, unfortunately. My route was Cafeteria -> Medbay -> back through Cafeteria -> Weapons. I never went into Electrical, and I didn\u2019t see Bob or Eve at all.\n\nThe main useful thing I can add is that if Bob really moved from Upper Engine toward Medbay around tick 6 like Charlie says, I did pass through Medbay and didn\u2019t see him, so timing matters there. But the bigger contradiction right now is Diana saying she was mostly Upper Engine/Oxygen and saw nobody, while Charlie says Bob was in Oxygen early and then Upper Engine. That\u2019s the only real mismatch we have.\n\nAlice reporting Eve in Electrical could be legit, but it\u2019s also the body location, so we can\u2019t fully clear her. Still, based on stories, Diana\u2019s route is the weakest match with what someone else saw. I\u2019m leaning Diana unless someone has a better explanation."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389079.483397, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "To answer Diana: no, I didn\u2019t see anyone hanging around Security, and I never went through Storage this round. My path was Navigation -> Security -> Electrical, and it was completely empty until I entered Electrical and found Eve\u2019s body.\n\nOn the stories: I agree the main mismatch is Diana saying she was Upper Engine/Oxygen but not seeing Bob, while Charlie says Bob was in Oxygen early and then Upper Engine toward Medbay. That could be timing, but it\u2019s the only direct contradiction so far.\n\nFrank being in Medbay is also worth noting because Bob was supposedly heading that way, but Frank didn\u2019t claim seeing him. For Eve specifically, I don\u2019t have anyone near Electrical besides me finding the body. I\u2019m leaning between Diana for the contradiction and Frank for Medbay timing, but Diana\u2019s story feels weaker right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389100.344812, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "\"Alice, Charlie, you guys need to think about this critically. Me not seeing Bob in Oxygen or Upper Engine is just a simple timing gap. If I was stuck doing a task or we missed each other by a couple of ticks, it\u2019s completely normal that we wouldn't cross paths. \n\nBut look closely at Frank's story! Charlie, you specifically said you saw Bob walk toward Medbay around tick 6. Frank just admitted he was walking through Medbay and claims he never saw Bob at all. How does that make sense? Bob was heading exactly to where Frank was! Frank being in the exact room Bob was heading to, but 'somehow' missing him, sounds exactly like a killer trying to distance himself from a body. \n\nIf we're voting based on who contradicts Charlie's sighting of Bob, Frank's contradiction is way worse because their paths directly overlap at the end of Bob's route. I'm voting Frank.\"\n\nvote: Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779389122.009438, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I want to be clear: my Bob info is solid \u2014 I saw him in Oxygen early, then at tick 6 I saw him leave Upper Engine toward Medbay. That doesn\u2019t mean he was instantly in Medbay; there\u2019s travel time, so Frank could have missed him if he passed through earlier.\n\nDiana\u2019s defense is possible, but her route is still the weirdest to me because Bob was on that left-side path for multiple ticks: Oxygen, then Upper Engine, then toward Medbay. If Diana was really mostly Oxygen/Upper Engine and saw nobody, that\u2019s a bigger mismatch than Frank not seeing Bob without exact timing.\n\nFor Eve, Alice finding in Electrical doesn\u2019t clear her, but her report and route are straightforward. Frank\u2019s Medbay path is worth noting, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s stronger than Diana\u2019s vague \u201cleft side\u201d claim not matching Bob\u2019s movement.\n\nI\u2019m still leaning Diana here unless Frank gives exact timing that sounds bad."}}
{"timestamp": 1779389146.7923908, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Diana, that push on me feels like deflection. Charlie even clarified the timing: Bob leaving Upper Engine toward Medbay at tick 6 doesn\u2019t mean he was standing in Medbay with me. I was not camped there \u2014 I passed through Medbay on my route Cafeteria -> Medbay -> back through Cafeteria -> Weapons, and I saw nobody.\n\nYour story is still the bigger issue because you said you were mostly Upper Engine and Oxygen, exactly the area where Charlie saw Bob multiple times, and you somehow saw nobody. That\u2019s a much wider overlap than me briefly passing through Medbay with uncertain timing.\n\nAlice\u2019s report on Eve in Electrical could be self-report, sure, but there\u2019s no contradiction there. Charlie\u2019s information has been the most specific, and it points more toward Diana than me.\n\nI\u2019m voting Diana."}}
